 @thomassmith4999  What the hell are you talking about?
The new consoles are not out, and there's been 0 announcements about a next gen RDR2 patch, much less performance details.
On consoles the game uses customized settings, mostly around Medium, some stuff is below PC's lowest settings.

 @cydia11centra  I know, that's why I said aside from Doom Eternal OR using DLSS/Dynamic Resolution scaling. Forza Horizon 4 was one that was tested, and that uses dynamic resolution rendering by default (pretty sure Linus/MKBHD didn't disable that). 
Edit: I'm pleasantly surprised to see that it was native 8k @ High preset. Still, 8k makes no sense in 2020 when we're still lacking solid 4k 120hz+ monitors lol

What other games have been tested and are able to run 60 fps @ 8k without setting the fidelity to "Low"?
